Now, we convert $B$ to Cartesian coordinates. To convert from polar coordinates to Cartesian coordinates, we use\n\n$$\nx=r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\nFirst, we calculate the $x$-coordinate of $B:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\   & =2\\cdot\\operatorname{cos}(\\frac{3\\pi}{2}) \\\\   & =2\\cdot(0) \\\\   & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we calculate the $y$-coordinate of $B:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\   & =2\\cdot\\operatorname{sin}(\\frac{3\\pi}{2}) \\\\   & =2\\cdot(-1) \\\\   & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the Cartesian coordinates of $B$ are $(0,-2).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["4514c27d-7de8-5fbe-af5b-39af5b0ac966"] :db/ensure :question/validate} {:db/id "641d2665-d10f-5535-ab2c-72bc489e588d" :answer/id #uuid "641d2665-d10f-5535-ab2c-72bc489e588d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(-8,0)" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "c248991e-d7e3-543a-bc27-44eb8bf16b56" :answer/id #uuid "c248991e-d7e3-543a-bc27-44eb8bf16b56" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(0,-8)" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "548319ac-3265-5a34-bb26-497ddb9afd2b" :answer/id #uuid "548319ac-3265-5a34-bb26-497ddb9afd2b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(-4,-4\\sqrt{3})" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "0b8f1b37-d179-55a2-8bdb-b8e5114e6a07" :answer/id #uuid "0b8f1b37-d179-55a2-8bdb-b8e5114e6a07" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(2,6)" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "c8056e82-36e7-5ff9-8524-d0cf2051f709" :answer/id #uuid "c8056e82-36e7-5ff9-8524-d0cf2051f709" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(4\\sqrt{3},-4)" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "7cc22fb0-8b96-50d7-81b9-3c21feb2ca19" :answer-field/id #uuid "7cc22fb0-8b96-50d7-81b9-3c21feb2ca19" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["641d2665-d10f-5535-